    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413-a1">

                <pb facs="1176" n="1170" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1170"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 8.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tracy to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                        1889</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith for
                    the information of the Department of State a copy of a report dated the 18th
                    ultimo from Rear-Admiral L. A. Kimberly, commanding the United States naval
                    force on the Pacific station, with reference to the political situation in the
                    Hawaiian Islands.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. F. Tracy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
